function pz_what_is_long_haired_cat_grooming() {
    ob_start(); ?>
    <p>This guide is built specifically around the challenge that defines long-haired cat care: mat prevention. Breeds like Persians, Maine Coons, and Ragdolls, along with any mixed-breed longhair, carry a dense undercoat that tangles far faster than a shorthaired coat ever does.</p>
    <p>Unlike shorthaired cats, where a weekly brush is often plenty, long-haired cats need daily attention. Skipping even a few days lets loose undercoat fur tangle into small knots that tighten every time the cat moves, eventually becoming mats that pull on the skin and may require a professional to remove.</p>
    <p>The approach here focuses on frequency and the right tools, since the single biggest factor in keeping a long-haired cat's coat healthy is consistency, not any one special technique.</p>
    <?php return ob_get_clean();
}

